# clause-codegen — backlog

## clause-jomini extension repo bootstrap

Post-R3 round: create the `clause-jomini` sibling repo with its
own mockspace, implementing `CodegenTarget` for Clausewitz script
output. Bind targets: Country, Pop, Planet, etc. (per
stellar-heritage/Python prior art). Landing in its own
orgrinrt/clause-jomini GitHub repo.

## Stage reordering via topological sort

Current `Stage` enum fixes the five-stage order (PreTypecheck →
PostTypecheck → CodegenPre → Codegen → Link). If a target needs
to declare "my stage X must happen before target Y's stage Z",
the schedule crate grows a target-stage dep resolver. Defer until
a concrete multi-target workflow surfaces the need.

## Target-provided lints

Targets may want to emit target-specific warnings during codegen
(e.g. Clausewitz-only "this pattern will OOM Stellaris at
runtime"). Current Diagnostic flow handles this via severity
tagging; a dedicated "lint scope" annotation could help IDEs
filter target-specific noise. Defer until a target surfaces
real need.

## SymbolRef cross-target resolution

R3 ships `SymbolRef` as the opaque type that targets use to
reference symbols across boundaries (clause-jomini references
clause-builtin symbols, etc.). The resolution ALGORITHM
(link-stage walker that matches SymbolRef producers ↔ consumers)
is deferred — first clause-jomini release will likely go without
cross-target references, and the algorithm lands when a concrete
need arrives.

## Multi-target parallel codegen

Current design is sequential: compile all units with target A,
then target B, etc. Parallel-codegen across targets (for
tooling-friendly UX) is a future optimisation — needs shared
ArtefactCache locking story.
